y.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Lane-scoped SASE_AGENT commit tag[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tag[dim] · [dim][/dim]after lanes[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tag: make the runtime commit-footer tag carry the lane label and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lane page destination, dropping the member anchor, for real commits, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PRs, and SDD auto-commits.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Lane-anchored sidecar publication requests[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]publish[dim] · [dim][/dim]after lanes[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]publish: record the lane as the publication identity in the outbox and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]make hood publication accept a lane name deliberately rather than by [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]accidental fallback.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Family containers carry their lane commits[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]snapshot[dim] · [dim][/dim]after lanes[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]snapshot: extend the v2 hood snapshot so family containers own [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lane-attributed commits, keep the strict decoder and import path in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agreement, and render them on the family page.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Lane-keyed commit history in the sidecar inventory[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]inventory[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tag, snapshot[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]inventory: read lane-tagged commit history, keep solo attribution [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unchanged, route family-lane commits to the family container, stop [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fabricating phantom runs, and keep import evidence matching.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Lane-based plan and bead agent associations[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]assoc[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tag[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]assoc: make plan-header and bead-page AGENTS rows label the lane once, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolve their link from the artifact member or the footer's recorded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]destination, and stop listing a member and its lane as two agents.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remaining SASE_AGENT tag readers and back-compat[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]consumers[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tag[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]consumers: make image-attachment scanning, revert discovery, and the PR [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]body footer lane-aware, and lock in that every reader still accepts [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]legacy member-name tags.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation refresh[/bold #D7AFFF]                                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tag, snapshot, inventory, assoc, consumers[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: update the commit-workflow, agents-sidecar, and SDD docs to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]describe lane-scoped provenance and the family page as the durable home [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]of a family's commits.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-b8","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-b8.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-f599d463d5cb785a8b4e811bfa13e829","started_at":"2026-07-30T14:34:25.405502+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-b8","bbug